  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EMPOWERING WEST AFRICAN WOMEN SMALL &amp; MEDIUM ENTERPRISES IN RICE VALUE CHAINS(EWASME) - Regional Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Empowering West African Womens Small and Medium Enterprises (EWASME) in the Rice Value Chain Program is a project aiming to improve and expand small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and very small enterprises (VSEs) owned or run by women, particularly at the post-production stage. This project aims to contribute to women&#x2019;s empowerment by strengthening the post-production capacity of at least 1,000 small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and very small enterprises (VSEs) run by women in</narrative>
  </description>
